From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH BlueZ 2/2] a2dp: Check setup->stream before setting the transport

transport_cb() already guards against the setup being freed while the
transport channel was being accepted:

	if (!g_slist_find(setups, setup)) {
		warn("bt_io_accept: setup %p no longer valid", setup);
		g_io_channel_shutdown(io, TRUE, NULL);
		return;
	}

but that only establishes that the setup itself is still on the list. It
does not establish that the setup still has a stream, and the value is
passed straight on:

	if (!avdtp_stream_set_transport(setup->stream, ...))

avdtp_stream_set_transport() dereferences its first argument in its
second statement, with no check of its own:

	GIOChannel *io = g_io_channel_unix_new(fd);

	if (stream != stream->session->pending_open) {

struct avdtp_stream has session at offset 0x10, so a NULL stream faults
reading address 0x10.

Observed three times on a QCA9377 (13d3:3503) whose controller stops
answering HCI during audio use, so the AVDTP session can be torn down
between bt_io_accept() and this callback firing. Resolved from the
shipped binary:

  bluetoothd[313564]: segfault at 10 ip 000060ff12be87e5 sp 00007fff35b2f190 \
      error 4 in bluetoothd[367e5,60ff12bd7000+f3000]

  #0  avdtp_stream_set_transport()  profiles/audio/avdtp.c  (inlined)
  #1  transport_cb()                profiles/audio/a2dp.c
  #2  accept_cb()                   btio/btio.c
  #3  glib main loop dispatch

  367e0:  e8 0b 12 ff ff    call   g_io_channel_unix_new@plt
  367e5:  49 8b 7d 10       mov    0x10(%r13),%rdi    <-- stream->session
  367ec:  48 8b 47 50       mov    0x50(%rdi),%rax    <-- session->pending_open
  367f0:  49 39 c5          cmp    %rax,%r13

Extend the existing validity check to cover the stream. avdtp_stream_set_-
transport() has exactly one caller, so the check is added here, next to
the check it completes, rather than hardening the callee.

Note this prevents the crash but does not explain why setup->stream is
cleared while the setup remains on the list; that is worth a separate
look by someone who knows the AVDTP teardown ordering.

Signed-off-by: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
---
 profiles/audio/a2dp.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/profiles/audio/a2dp.c b/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
--- a/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
+++ b/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
@@ -2652,6 +2652,11 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
+	if (!setup->stream) {
+		error("bt_io_accept: setup %p has no stream", setup);
+		goto drop;
+	}
+
 	if (err) {
 		error("%s", err->message);
 		goto drop;
-- 
